Static binaries. No library dependencies, they run on any x86_64 Linux
with X11 (glibc or musl based, any release).

  install -Dm755 nightlightd     ~/.local/bin/nightlightd
  install -Dm755 nightlight-tui  ~/.local/bin/nightlight-tui
  install -Dm644 nightlightd.service ~/.config/systemd/user/nightlightd.service
  systemctl --user daemon-reload
  systemctl --user enable --now nightlightd

The bundled service file starts %h/.local/bin/nightlightd, which is where
the lines above put it. If you install the binary somewhere else, edit
ExecStart to match.

This tarball carries the daemon and the terminal dashboard only. The tray
icon and the settings panel need a graphical toolkit and cannot be built
static, so they are in the .deb and the AUR package instead.
